Z||000000||GodSend||08-20-2000||02:46 AM||||  Anyone know a good place to splice into to get the hazard lights to flash when I arm/disarm.  Im looking for 12+ when on and 0 when off .  I was looking at splicing in directly to the hazard plug but I can't figure out how to get into the steering column.<P>GodSend||||reg||1
Z||000001||Xtreme Fiero's||08-20-2000||09:35 AM||||look in a haynes manual to figure out what collor wire you are looking for and look for it at the base of the column. I also think there is a screw in the canter of the hazard switch that mey remove it but im no sure. hope i helped.||||reg||1
Z||000002||cifc||08-20-2000||10:51 AM||||Pull out your headlight switch.  YOu should see a brown wire back there.  That should be the one you need.  test it first.  should read 12v with the parking lights on.<BR>--Jason||||reg||1
Z||000003||sluppy123||08-20-2000||10:58 PM||||I'll second cifc, It's the Brown wire on the back of the headlight switch.<P><P>------------------<BR>-Brian S.<BR>Lincoln, NE<BR>85' SC & 87' GT||||reg||1
